# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        name: "Boomlify"
        url: "https://boomlify.com"
      }
      description: "Generate millions of temp mail from boomlify. A free temporary email service that allows you to create disposable email addresses instantly with custom domain support, extended validity (2+ months), and professional business email solutions."
      servers: [
        {
          description: "Production server"
          url: "https://api.boomlify.com/v1"
        }
      ]
      termsOfService: "https://boomlify.com/terms"
      title: "Temp Mail API"
      version: "1.0.0"
      tagline: "Generate disposable email addresses and read incoming messages via Boomlify's temp mail API"
      homepage: "https://boomlify.com"
      docs_url: "https://boomlify.com"
      about_md: `[Boomlify](https://boomlify.com) is a temporary email service that lets you create disposable inbox addresses on demand. This SDK wraps its public API, served from \`https://api.boomlify.com/v1\`, so you can integrate ephemeral mail flows into automated signups, testing pipelines, or privacy-sensitive workflows.

The service is aimed at avoiding spam, protecting your real address when trying out services, and giving developers a way to verify email-based flows without burning real inboxes. Boomlify also advertises support for custom domains and a multi-inbox dashboard on its consumer site.

Use the API to mint a new temporary email address and poll its inbox for messages. Refer to Boomlify's own site for the canonical authentication, rate-limit, and retention details.`
      entity_desc: {
        temporary_email: "A disposable email address minted by Boomlify, along with the messages delivered to it; covered by the SDK operations grouped under the `temporary_email` entity."
      }
      auth: false
    }
  }
}
